BG_T="Background: genuinely TRANSPARENT (real alpha), no background colour, no ground, no sky."
BG_K="Background: pure solid black #000000 everywhere except the glowing element (light sources are drawn additively over the game, so the element's brightness is its opacity); no ground, no sky, no stars."
rain() { echo "RAIN FLOW STRIP SOURCE: a transparent RGBA overlay of realistic wind-driven rain over the whole square, to be tiled as a seamless scrolling layer. $BG_T Content: slanted thin rain streaks (about 17 degrees from vertical, leaning right) at three depth scales: many fine, faint, short far streaks; fewer medium streaks; a few longer, brighter near streaks; irregular spacing like real rain; faint translucent grey-blue spray and wind-dragged mist wisps; tiny splash flecks. Cool desaturated steel-blue/white at LOW opacity: this is a subtle layer, LESS HAZY than a mist veil (no big soft fog patches, no opaque areas), only about 5 to 10 percent of pixels non-transparent. The central 40 percent of the width stays much sparser than the sides. Every streak and wisp lies fully INSIDE the frame with at least 40 px margin to all four edges (nothing is cut by an edge). Character of this source: $1"; }
